    reality: 'Warehouse, dispatch, and last-mile operations roles at e-commerce and 3PL companies sit here — pay varies significantly by company size and city tier.',
  },
  {
    stage: 'Supply chain/planning analyst, 2-5 years',
    range: 'Rs 6-12 LPA',
    reality: 'Requires genuine data and Excel/analytics fluency; MBA-qualified candidates or those with a demonstrated analytical track record sit toward the upper end.',
  },
  {
    stage: 'Logistics/operations manager, 5-10 years',
    range: 'Rs 12-22 LPA',
    reality: 'Requires real P&L or vendor-network ownership, not just team supervision — the jump to this tier is a scope jump, not a tenure milestone.',
  },
  {
    stage: 'Senior supply chain leader/head of logistics, 10+ years',
    range: 'Rs 25-45 LPA and above',
    reality: 'Concentrated at large e-commerce, manufacturing, and FMCG companies with complex, multi-region supply chains — this tier requires genuine strategic and cross-functional leadership.',
  },
  {
    stage: 'Freight forwarding/customs and international logistics specialist',
    range: 'Rs 5-15 LPA depending on experience',
    reality: 'A genuinely differentiated niche within logistics, requiring specific regulatory and documentation expertise that is scarcer than generalist domestic operations skill.',
  },
];

const automationComparison = {
  gold: [
    'Warehouse automation — robotics, automated sorting, and route-optimisation software — has genuinely reduced headcount needs for the most repetitive physical and manual-scheduling tasks at large-scale operations.',
    'AI-driven demand forecasting and route planning are automating parts of what used to be manual analyst work, particularly at large e-commerce and logistics-tech companies investing heavily in these systems.',
    'Basic data-entry and tracking-status coordination roles, once a common entry point into logistics, are shrinking as tracking and status updates become increasingly automated end to end.',
  ],
  teal: [
    'Physical movement of goods still requires real-world coordination — vendor relationships, exception handling when something genuinely goes wrong, and on-ground problem-solving that automated systems cannot yet fully replace.',
    'India\'s logistics sector overall is still growing with e-commerce, manufacturing (China-plus-one shifts), and infrastructure investment (dedicated freight corridors, port modernisation) outpacing the efficiency gains automation delivers.',
    'Demand for people who can manage complex vendor networks, negotiate contracts, and make judgment calls during genuine supply-chain disruptions is rising, not falling — automation handles the routine; humans still own the exceptions and the strategy.',
  ],
};

const growthCards = [
  {
    title: 'Move from execution roles into planning and analytics as early as possible',
    body: 'Warehouse and operations execution roles have a lower ceiling and more automation exposure than planning, forecasting, and analytics roles — moving upstream is the clearest path to both higher pay and more durable relevance.',
