    body: 'Modern supply chain roles increasingly reward people who can work with forecasting tools, inventory-optimisation software, and basic data analysis — operational experience alone has a real, moderate ceiling without this layered on.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Specialise in a scarce niche: international freight, customs/regulatory compliance, or cold-chain logistics',
    body: 'Generalist domestic logistics experience is common; genuine expertise in international freight documentation, customs regulation, or temperature-controlled cold-chain operations commands a real premium.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Pursue a formal supply chain management qualification once you have real operational grounding',
    body: 'An MBA or postgraduate supply chain management qualification, layered on top of genuine operational experience rather than in place of it, meaningfully accelerates the path into leadership roles.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Build cross-functional fluency with procurement, finance, and sales, not logistics alone',
    body: 'Senior supply chain leadership roles require working across procurement, finance, and sales functions — building that cross-functional fluency early differentiates candidates aiming for leadership from those who stay purely operational.',
  },
];

const whoFitsItems = [
  {
    label: 'Genuine fit',
    title: 'You are comfortable with real-time problem-solving when things genuinely go wrong',
    body: 'Logistics work regularly involves disruptions — a delayed shipment, a vendor issue, a weather event — that need immediate, practical judgment calls. If staying calm and solving problems under time pressure appeals to you, that is a real signal.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Genuine fit',
    title: 'You want a field with genuinely broad entry routes and real growth headroom for people who move deliberately',
    body: 'Logistics has functional entry routes from operations-floor roles through to MBA-qualified planning and leadership roles — useful for people without a specific specialised degree, provided they plan a deliberate move upstream.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Genuine fit',
    title: 'You are willing to build genuine data and analytical fluency over time, not stay purely operational',
    body: 'The field is increasingly rewarding data-literate professionals over purely execution-focused ones. Comfort with continuous skill-building toward analytics and planning is a real asset here.',
  },
];

const whoPauseRows = [
  {
    signal: 'You are entering purely execution-focused warehouse or dispatch roles with no plan to move upstream',
    reality: 'These roles have the lowest pay ceiling and the highest automation exposure in the field. A realistic plan should include a deliberate path toward planning, analytics, or management within a few years.',
  },
  {
    signal: 'You are avoiding the field because "logistics is getting automated" without checking which parts specifically',
    reality: 'Automation is genuinely reducing headcount for repetitive physical and manual-scheduling tasks, but overall sector growth from e-commerce and manufacturing expansion is outpacing those efficiency gains. The honest read is a shifting skill mix, not a shrinking field.',
