  },
  {
    num: '05',
    title: 'Choosing an expensive logistics/supply chain management programme without checking its actual placement track record',
    body: 'A useful discipline: treat roughly 10% of your total education budget as the default starting benchmark for programme spend, and check any shortlisted programme\'s real, verifiable placement outcomes before spending materially above that.',
  },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Is logistics a good career in India in 2026?',
    a: 'Yes, for people willing to build a deliberate path from operational execution toward planning, analytics, or management over time. Logistics in India spans warehouse and dispatch operations executives (Rs 2.5-5 LPA entry-level) through to senior supply chain leaders at large e-commerce and manufacturing companies (Rs 25-45 LPA and above). The sector overall is genuinely growing with e-commerce and manufacturing expansion, but automation is genuinely reducing demand for the most repetitive physical and manual-scheduling roles specifically.',
